 ("note", "DEFINITION", "**Governance** is the system through which decisions are made, implemented and monitored for the welfare of people. Democratic governance rests on transparency, accountability, participation and the rule of law."),
 ("p", "Example: a panchayat is the government that installs street lights; governance is the planning, repair and feedback process, with people reporting dark spots."),
 ("h2", "Evolution of Governance in India"),
 ("ul", ["Colonial rule imposed its own models, and many colonial institutions continued after independence. India kept much knowledge of pre-colonial traditions, and the Constitution was framed in the spirit of Indian values.", "**Satyameva Jayate** (Munḍaka Upaniṣhad) is the national motto; the Supreme Court's motto **Yato Dharmastato Jayaḥ** comes from the Mahābhārata.", "The **Sengol**, a Chola-era symbol of righteous rule, was received by Nehru in 1947 and placed in the new Parliament in 2023.", "Gandhi's ideal was **Rām Rājya**: probity, transparency, compassion and welfare.", "**Rājadharma** was the king's duty to protect people and uphold Dharma. Kauṭilya says the king's happiness lies in the people's happiness. The Ṛigveda mentions the **Sabhā and Samiti**."]),
 ("h2", "Good Governance"),
 ("table", ["Feature", "Meaning"], [["Rule of law", "Everyone is equal before the law"], ["Accountability", "Officials answer for their actions"], ["Participation", "Citizens take part in decisions"], ["Transparency", "Decisions are open and accessible"], ["Effectiveness", "Public resources are used wisely"], ["Responsiveness", "Government addresses people's needs"], ["Inclusiveness", "Every citizen has equal opportunities"]]),
 ("ul", ["Good governance keeps law and order, protects rights, delivers services and builds trust.", "Government makes laws and policies; citizens vote, obey laws and participate; media informs; civil society raises awareness; the private sector adds economic activity.", "**Challenges:** weak coordination, unequal access to services, misuse of office, fake news.", "25 December is observed as **National Good Governance Day**."]),
 ("h2", "E-Governance"),
 ("p", "**E-governance** is the use of information and communication technology to provide services, share information, receive feedback and improve administration. It reduces paperwork and saves visits to offices."),
 ("table", ["Initiative", "Purpose"], [["UMANG", "Many government services on one platform"], ["Aadhaar", "Unique identity"], ["GeM", "Government e-Marketplace for purchases"], ["DigiLocker", "Digital storage of documents"], ["CPGRAMS", "Public grievances"], ["APAAR", "Education-related digital identity"]]),
 ("note", "IMPORTANT", "E-governance works only with devices, internet and digital skills, so services must stay inclusive."),
 ("h2", "Public Policy"),
 ("note", "DEFINITION", "**Public policy** is a course of action adopted by the government to solve public problems, meet needs and promote welfare. It decides what to do, why, who, how and how success is measured."),
 ("ul", ["‘Public’: made for public benefit, carried out by public institutions, financed by public money, and shaped by people.", "A school, company or housing society also has policies, but they apply to limited groups and are not public policy."]),
 ("table", ["Stakeholder", "Role", "Example"], [["Citizens", "Identify problems, vote, give feedback", "Residents ask for a zebra crossing"], ["Elected representatives", "Raise issues, make laws, approve budgets", "MLA raises water shortage"], ["Officials, departments", "Prepare, implement, monitor", "District collector coordinates a scheme"], ["Civil society, media, experts", "Study, create awareness, monitor", "NGO runs a water campaign"], ["Private sector", "Resources, innovation", "Solar panels via PPP"], ["International organisations", "Experience, technical and financial help", "WHO and disease control"]]),
